{%- comment -%}
  One photograph in a product card's media stack.

  Only the first two carry a real `src`. Slide 0 is what the card shows and
  slide 1 is what hover previews, so those two are the entire experience for a
  visitor without scripting — the arrows do nothing without it. Every slide
  after them is deferred behind `data-src`, and theme.js fetches it when the
  card first steps to it.

  That is what lets a piece carry a hundred photographs. A slide is `opacity: 0`,
  not `display: none`, so the browser treats it as visible and fetches it with
  the rest of the card however far down the stack it sits — a hundred slides
  would be a hundred requests per card, times every card in the grid.

  `blurUp()` binds its load listener before any of this is swapped in, so a
  deferred slide still fades up from the design's blur when it arrives.

  Accepts:
    media   - product media object, of type image.
    index   - position in the card's slide order, 0-based.
    eager   - true when the browser should fetch it up front.
    product - for the alt fallback.
    sizes   - sizes attribute.
    loading - loading attribute.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign src = media | image_url: width: 800
  assign w300 = media | image_url: width: 300
  assign w600 = media | image_url: width: 600
  assign w900 = media | image_url: width: 900
  assign w1200 = media | image_url: width: 1200
  assign alt_text = media.alt | default: product.title | escape
-%}

{%- capture srcset -%}
  {{ w300 }} 300w, {{ w600 }} 600w, {{ w900 }} 900w, {{ w1200 }} 1200w
{%- endcapture -%}

<span class="card__slide{% if index == 0 %} is-on{% endif %}" data-card-slide="{{ index }}">
  <img
    class="card__img"
    {% if eager %}
      src="{{ src }}"
      srcset="{{ srcset }}"
    {% else %}
      data-src="{{ src }}"
      data-srcset="{{ srcset }}"
    {% endif %}
    sizes="{{ sizes }}"
    alt="{{ alt_text }}"
    width="{{ media.width }}"
    height="{{ media.height }}"
    loading="{{ loading }}"
    decoding="async"
    data-card-blur
  >
</span>
